  "note": "First election of the urban district council; poll for the whole town on Monday 16 January 1899, counted 17 January. \"The Unionist candidates were, with one exception, all successful\"; individual party labels are not printed. Electorate \"about 2,700\"; 1,323 voted; eleven spoilt papers. Dr. Moore's forename is not given (in 1911 a Dr. J. M. Moore sat for Lurgan)."
